{"name":"Kangaroo Paw","hex":"#decac5","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"kangaroo paw","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of various perennial flowering plants of the family Haemodoraceae, endemic to the south-west of Western Australia."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/kangaroo_paw"}],"entries":[{"title":"Kangaroo paw","blocks":[{"text":"Kangaroo paw is the common name for a number of species, in two genera of the family Haemodoraceae, that are native to the south-west of Western Australia. These rhizomatous perennial plants are noted for their unique bird-attracting flowers. The tubular flowers are coated with dense hairs and open at the apex with six claw-like structures which resemble kangaroo forelimbs, and it is from this paw-like formation that the common name \"kangaroo paw\" is derived."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/08/Kangaroo_paw_260920_gnangarra_15_years-101.jpg/330px-Kangaroo_paw_260920_gnangarra_15_years-101.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kangaroo_paw","wikidata":"Q1967491"},{"title":"Kangaroo","blocks":[{"text":"Kangaroos are marsupials from the subfamily Macropodinae. In common use, the term is used to describe the largest species from this family, the red kangaroo, as well as the antilopine kangaroo, eastern grey kangaroo, and western grey kangaroo. Kangaroos are indigenous to Australia and New Guinea. The Australian government estimated that 42.8 million kangaroos lived within the commercial harvest areas of Australia in 2019, down from 53.2 million in 2013."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/df/Forester_kangaroo_%28Macropus_giganteus_tasmaniensis%29_juvenile_hopping_Esk_Valley.jpg/330px-Forester_kangaroo_%28Macropus_giganteus_tasmaniensis%29_juvenile_hopping_Esk_Valley.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kangaroo","wikidata":"Q5070208"},{"title":"Paw","blocks":[{"text":"A paw is the soft foot-like part of a mammal, generally a quadruped, that has claws. To paw is for an animal to use their paws, usually gently or for digging, or for a human to use their hands in the manner of an animal's paw."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8d/Paw_and_pads.jpg/330px-Paw_and_pads.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Paw","wikidata":"Q219588"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/12/Anigozanthos_flavidus_close-up.jpg/500px-Anigozanthos_flavidus_close-up.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/12/Anigozanthos_flavidus_close-up.jpg/500px-Anigozanthos_flavidus_close-up.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Anigozanthos flavidus","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAnigozanthos_flavidus_close-up.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4c/Macropidia_fulginosa_SMC.JPG/500px-Macropidia_fulginosa_SMC.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4c/Macropidia_fulginosa_SMC.JPG/1280px-Macropidia_fulginosa_SMC.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4c/Macropidia_fulginosa_SMC.JPG/500px-Macropidia_fulginosa_SMC.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Macropidia fuliginosa","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMacropidia_fulginosa_SMC.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/06/Anigozanthos_humilis_Gnangarra-11.jpg/500px-Anigozanthos_humilis_Gnangarra-11.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&